      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While tax cuts favoring capital gains have been a significant contributor, they are not the sole cause. Labor market shifts, such as the decline in unionization and wage stagnation for many workers, also play a crucial role. Additionally, changes in financialization and asset price inflation—which benefits those who already own assets—magnify the gap. Therefore, it's best to view it as a combination of fiscal policy and structural economic changes working together.",
